  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest performance jump so far came from switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_036: 0.6390 → config_038: 0.6776, with resnet50/avgpool/weighted). Meanwhile, pca_n2000 shows near-parity between imagenet_vit_l (0.6352) and resnet50 (0.6390). Question: Does the scvi_n200 improvement generalize to imagenet_vit_l, or is it specific to the resnet50 pairing? Testing config_001 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) completes a clean 2×2 factorial over {pca_n2000, scvi_n200} × {resnet50, imagenet_vit_l} with all other factors held constant, isolating the RNA-encoder and image-encoder main effects and their interaction. Why best next: It is a single-variable change from the current best (config_038), directly extends the strongest evidence, and the resulting 2×2 will clarify whether to invest further in scvi_n200 broadly or only in specific pairings—critical information before spending budget on aggregation/fusion variants."
}

